-- title:
--   Level sums of Fourier coefficients as biased expectations
-- statement:
--   Let $g:\{0,1\}^m\to\mathbb R$ and let $\Lambda_l(g)=\sum_{|t|=l}\hat g(t)$ be the total Fourier mass at degree $l$. For $x\in\mathbb R$ let $\mathbb E_x$ denote the biased expectation with weights $\prod_i\frac{1+x\,\mathrm{sgn}(\varepsilon_i)}2$, where $\mathrm{sgn}(0)=1$, $\mathrm{sgn}(1)=-1$. Then
--   $$
--   \sum_{l=0}^m\Lambda_l(g)\,x^l=\mathbb E_x\,g .
--   $$
--
--   The generating function of the level sums is the expectation under independent coordinates of bias $x$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/ProjectionDerivatives.lean#L20-L39

